Hazards of Grinding Machines

Grinding machines primarily alter the size, shape, and surface finish of metal by placing a work-piece against a rotating abrasive surface or wheel. Grind- ing machines may also be used for grinding glass, ceramics, plastics, and rubber.

Examples of grinding machines include abrasive belt machines, abrasive cutoff machines, cylindrical grinders, centerless grinders, gear grinders, internal grinders, lapping machines, off-hand grinders, sur- face grinders, swing frame grinders, and thread grinders. (See Figure 42.)

